WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — rce-compile (60s) Narrator Lem

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.927
RCE Compile tests a single candidate statement across GCC,

2
00:00:05.927 --> 00:00:11.920
Clang, Rustc, CompCert, MLIR, JITs, and hardware synthesizers.

3
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:16.328
Existing compilers omit explicit gates and reuse keys;

4
00:00:16.328 --> 00:00:22.303
restating compilation as a seven-part normal form makes every assumption checkable.

5
00:00:22.823 --> 00:00:27.673
Moving from Python to Clang O3 pays back in 2,490 runs,

6
00:00:27.673 --> 00:00:33.581
whereas O2-to-O3 fails to pay back in 30 percent of measured pairs.

7
00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:42.483
Naive AST identifier stripping mis-caches 150 of 500 variable-capture mutants;

8
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:47.534
De Bruijn canonical SHA-256 scores zero errors.

9
00:00:48.054 --> 00:00:55.704
Safe alpha-equivalent artifact reuse collapses warm compilation reported_j by two orders of magnitude.
